# Grammaire anglaise, expliquée dans les autres langues d'interface.
T = {
'pronunciation': {
 'es': ('Pronunciación y ortografía', "La ortografía inglesa refleja mal la pronunciación: una letra tiene varios sonidos (cat, cake, car, call) y un sonido varias grafías (see, sea, me, piece). Aprende cada palabra con su pronunciación.\nSonidos típicos: «th» (think, sordo; this, sonoro), vocales breves y largas que distinguen palabras (ship / sheep, full / fool), «h» siempre aspirada (house), «r» sin vibrar.\nLetras mudas: know, write, hour, island.\nLa terminación -ed suena /t/ tras un sonido sordo (worked), /d/ tras uno sonoro (played), /ɪd/ tras t o d (wanted).\nEl inglés acentúa las palabras importantes y reduce las pequeñas: «to», «of», «and» se vuelven muy breves.", ['Creo que este es el tercero.', 'Sé la respuesta.']),
 'de': ('Aussprache und Rechtschreibung', "Die englische Schreibung gibt die Aussprache schlecht wieder: Ein Buchstabe hat mehrere Laute (cat, cake, car, call), ein Laut mehrere Schreibweisen (see, sea, me, piece). Lerne jedes Wort mit seiner Aussprache.\nTypische Laute: „th“ (think, stimmlos; this, stimmhaft), kurze und lange Vokale, die Wörter unterscheiden (ship / sheep, full / fool), „h“ immer gehaucht (house), ungerolltes „r“.\nStumme Buchstaben: know, write, hour, island.\nDie Endung -ed klingt /t/ nach stimmlosem Laut (worked), /d/ nach stimmhaftem (played), /ɪd/ nach t oder d (wanted).\nDas Englische betont die wichtigen Wörter und verkürzt die kleinen: „to“, „of“, „and“ werden sehr kurz.", ['Ich glaube, das ist der dritte.', 'Ich kenne die Antwort.']),
 'it': ('Pronuncia e ortografia', "L'ortografia inglese rende male la pronuncia: una lettera ha più suoni (cat, cake, car, call) e un suono più grafie (see, sea, me, piece). Impara ogni parola con la sua pronuncia.\nSuoni tipici: «th» (think, sordo; this, sonoro), vocali brevi e lunghe che distinguono le parole (ship / sheep, full / fool), «h» sempre aspirata (house), «r» non vibrata.\nLettere mute: know, write, hour, island.\nLa desinenza -ed si pronuncia /t/ dopo un suono sordo (worked), /d/ dopo uno sonoro (played), /ɪd/ dopo t o d (wanted).\nL'inglese accentua le parole importanti e riduce quelle piccole: «to», «of», «and» diventano brevissime.", ['Penso che questo sia il terzo.', 'So la risposta.']),
 'pt': ('Pronúncia e ortografia', "A ortografia inglesa reflete mal a pronúncia: uma letra tem vários sons (cat, cake, car, call) e um som várias grafias (see, sea, me, piece). Aprenda cada palavra com sua pronúncia.\nSons típicos: «th» (think, surdo; this, sonoro), vogais curtas e longas que distinguem palavras (ship / sheep, full / fool), «h» sempre aspirado (house), «r» sem vibração.\nLetras mudas: know, write, hour, island.\nA terminação -ed soa /t/ depois de som surdo (worked), /d/ depois de som sonoro (played), /ɪd/ depois de t ou d (wanted).\nO inglês acentua as palavras importantes e reduz as pequenas: «to», «of», «and» ficam muito curtas.", ['Acho que este é o terceiro.', 'Eu sei a resposta.']),
 'ja': ('発音とつづり', "英語のつづりは発音をよく表していません。一つの文字に複数の音があり（cat, cake, car, call）、一つの音に複数のつづりがあります（see, sea, me, piece）。単語は発音といっしょに覚えましょう。\n英語らしい音：「th」（think は無声、this は有声）、語を区別する短母音と長母音（ship / sheep, full / fool）、いつも息を出す「h」（house）、巻かない「r」。\n発音しない文字：know, write, hour, island。\n語尾 -ed は無声音の後で /t/（worked）、有声音の後で /d/（played）、t・d の後で /ɪd/（wanted）。\n英語は大事な語を強く、小さな語を弱く発音します。「to」「of」「and」はとても短くなります。", ['これは3番目だと思います。', '答えを知っています。']),
 'zh': ('发音与拼写', "英语拼写不能很好地反映发音：一个字母有多种读音（cat, cake, car, call），一个音有多种拼法（see, sea, me, piece）。每个单词都要连同发音一起记。\n英语特有的音：「th」（think 清音，this 浊音），区分词义的长短元音（ship / sheep, full / fool），总要送气的「h」（house），不打舌的「r」。\n不发音的字母：know, write, hour, island。\n词尾 -ed 在清音后读 /t/（worked），在浊音后读 /d/（played），在 t、d 后读 /ɪd/（wanted）。\n英语重读重要的词，弱读小词：「to」「of」「and」会读得很短。", ['我想这是第三个。', '我知道答案。']),
 'ko': ('발음과 철자', "영어 철자는 발음을 잘 나타내지 못합니다. 한 글자에 여러 소리가 있고(cat, cake, car, call), 한 소리에 여러 철자가 있습니다(see, sea, me, piece). 단어는 발음과 함께 외우세요.\n영어다운 소리: 「th」(think는 무성음, this는 유성음), 뜻을 구별하는 짧은 모음과 긴 모음(ship / sheep, full / fool), 항상 숨을 내쉬는 「h」(house), 굴리지 않는 「r」.\n소리 나지 않는 글자: know, write, hour, island.\n어미 -ed는 무성음 뒤에서 /t/(worked), 유성음 뒤에서 /d/(played), t나 d 뒤에서 /ɪd/(wanted)로 소리 납니다.\n영어는 중요한 단어를 강하게, 작은 단어를 약하게 발음합니다. 「to」, 「of」, 「and」는 아주 짧아집니다.", ['이게 세 번째인 것 같아요.', '저는 답을 알아요.']),
 'lt': ('Tarimas ir rašyba', "Anglų rašyba prastai atspindi tarimą: viena raidė turi kelis garsus (cat, cake, car, call), vienas garsas – kelias rašybas (see, sea, me, piece). Kiekvieną žodį mokykitės kartu su tarimu.\nBūdingi garsai: „th“ (think – duslus, this – skardus), trumpieji ir ilgieji balsiai, skiriantys žodžius (ship / sheep, full / fool), visada aspiruotas „h“ (house), nevirpinamas „r“.\nNetariamos raidės: know, write, hour, island.\nGalūnė -ed tariama /t/ po duslaus garso (worked), /d/ po skardaus (played), /ɪd/ po t arba d (wanted).\nAnglai kirčiuoja svarbius žodžius, o mažuosius ištaria labai trumpai: „to“, „of“, „and“.", ['Manau, kad tai trečias.', 'Aš žinau atsakymą.']),
 'tl': ('Pagbigkas at baybay', "Hindi tapat ang baybay ng Ingles sa bigkas: isang titik ay may ilang tunog (cat, cake, car, call) at isang tunog ay may ilang baybay (see, sea, me, piece). Pag-aralan ang bawat salita kasama ang bigkas nito.\nMga karaniwang tunog: «th» (think, walang tinig; this, may tinig), maikli at mahabang patinig na nag-iiba ng salita (ship / sheep, full / fool), «h» na laging may hininga (house), «r» na hindi pinapagulong.\nMga titik na hindi binibigkas: know, write, hour, island.\nAng hulaping -ed ay /t/ pagkatapos ng tunog na walang tinig (worked), /d/ pagkatapos ng may tinig (played), /ɪd/ pagkatapos ng t o d (wanted).\nDiniinan ng Ingles ang mahahalagang salita at pinaiikli ang maliliit: «to», «of», «and».", ['Sa tingin ko ito ang ikatlo.', 'Alam ko ang sagot.']),
},
'be': {
 'es': ('El verbo «be» en presente', "«Be» (ser / estar) tiene tres formas en presente: I am, he / she / it is, you / we / they are. Al hablar se contraen: I'm, you're, he's, we're, they're.\nNegación: se añade «not» (is not = isn't, are not = aren't). Pregunta: se invierte verbo y sujeto (Are you ready?).\nEl inglés usa «be» para la edad, el hambre y el frío: I am twenty, I am hungry, I am cold.", ['Soy estudiante.', 'Ella no está en casa.', '¿Son tus amigos?']),
 'de': ('Das Verb „be“ im Präsens', "„Be“ (sein) hat drei Präsensformen: I am, he / she / it is, you / we / they are. Gesprochen wird zusammengezogen: I'm, you're, he's, we're, they're.\nVerneinung: „not“ anhängen (is not = isn't, are not = aren't). Frage: Verb und Subjekt tauschen (Are you ready?).\nEnglisch benutzt „be“ für Alter, Hunger und Kälte: I am twenty, I am hungry, I am cold.", ['Ich bin Student.', 'Sie ist nicht zu Hause.', 'Sind das deine Freunde?']),
 'it': ('Il verbo «be» al presente', "«Be» (essere) ha tre forme al presente: I am, he / she / it is, you / we / they are. Parlando si contrae: I'm, you're, he's, we're, they're.\nNegazione: si aggiunge «not» (is not = isn't, are not = aren't). Domanda: si invertono verbo e soggetto (Are you ready?).\nL'inglese usa «be» per l'età, la fame e il freddo: I am twenty, I am hungry, I am cold.", ['Sono uno studente.', 'Lei non è a casa.', 'Sono i tuoi amici?']),
 'pt': ('O verbo «be» no presente', "«Be» (ser / estar) tem três formas no presente: I am, he / she / it is, you / we / they are. Na fala contraem-se: I'm, you're, he's, we're, they're.\nNegação: acrescenta-se «not» (is not = isn't, are not = aren't). Pergunta: inverte-se verbo e sujeito (Are you ready?).\nO inglês usa «be» para idade, fome e frio: I am twenty, I am hungry, I am cold.", ['Sou estudante.', 'Ela não está em casa.', 'São seus amigos?']),
 'ja': ('be動詞（現在形）', "「be」（〜である、〜にいる）は現在形に三つの形があります：I am、he / she / it is、you / we / they are。話し言葉では短くなります：I'm, you're, he's, we're, they're。\n否定は「not」をつけます（is not = isn't, are not = aren't）。疑問文は動詞と主語を入れかえます（Are you ready?）。\n年齢・空腹・寒さにも be を使います：I am twenty, I am hungry, I am cold。", ['私は学生です。', '彼女は家にいません。', '彼らはあなたの友達ですか？']),
 'zh': ('动词 be 的现在时', "「be」（是、在）现在时有三种形式：I am，he / she / it is，you / we / they are。口语中常缩写：I'm, you're, he's, we're, they're。\n否定：加「not」（is not = isn't，are not = aren't）。疑问：把动词和主语调换位置（Are you ready?）。\n英语用 be 表达年龄、饥饿和寒冷：I am twenty, I am hungry, I am cold。", ['我是学生。', '她不在家。', '他们是你的朋友吗？']),
 'ko': ('be 동사의 현재형', "「be」(~이다, ~에 있다)는 현재형이 셋입니다: I am, he / she / it is, you / we / they are. 말할 때는 줄여 씁니다: I'm, you're, he's, we're, they're.\n부정: 「not」을 붙입니다(is not = isn't, are not = aren't). 의문문: 동사와 주어의 자리를 바꿉니다(Are you ready?).\n나이, 배고픔, 추위에도 be를 씁니다: I am twenty, I am hungry, I am cold.", ['저는 학생이에요.', '그녀는 집에 없어요.', '그들이 당신 친구들이에요?']),
 'lt': ('Veiksmažodis „be“ esamuoju laiku', "„Be“ (būti) esamajame laike turi tris formas: I am, he / she / it is, you / we / they are. Šnekant sutrumpinama: I'm, you're, he's, we're, they're.\nNeiginys: pridedamas „not“ (is not = isn't, are not = aren't). Klausimas: sukeičiami veiksmažodis ir veiksnys (Are you ready?).\nAnglai vartoja „be“ amžiui, alkiui ir šalčiui: I am twenty, I am hungry, I am cold.", ['Aš esu studentas.', 'Jos nėra namie.', 'Ar jie tavo draugai?']),
 'tl': ('Ang pandiwang «be» sa kasalukuyan', "Ang «be» ay may tatlong anyo sa kasalukuyan: I am, he / she / it is, you / we / they are. Sa pagsasalita, pinaiikli: I'm, you're, he's, we're, they're.\nNegatibo: idagdag ang «not» (is not = isn't, are not = aren't). Tanong: pagpalitin ang pandiwa at simuno (Are you ready?).\nGinagamit ang «be» para sa edad, gutom at lamig: I am twenty, I am hungry, I am cold.", ['Estudyante ako.', 'Wala siya sa bahay.', 'Mga kaibigan mo ba sila?']),
},
'articles': {
 'es': ('Los artículos: a, an, the', "«A» delante de un sonido consonántico (a book, a university), «an» delante de un sonido vocálico (an apple, an hour). Significan «un, una» y solo se usan en singular.\n«The» (el, la, los, las) nunca cambia. Se usa para lo conocido o ya mencionado.\nSin artículo para hablar en general: I like music. Dogs are friendly.", ['Tengo un perro y un paraguas.', 'El perro está en el jardín.', 'Me encanta el café.']),
 'de': ('Die Artikel: a, an, the', "„A“ vor einem Konsonantenlaut (a book, a university), „an“ vor einem Vokallaut (an apple, an hour). Sie bedeuten „ein, eine“ und stehen nur im Singular.\n„The“ (der, die, das) ändert sich nie. Man benutzt es für Bekanntes oder schon Erwähntes.\nKein Artikel bei allgemeinen Aussagen: I like music. Dogs are friendly.", ['Ich habe einen Hund und einen Regenschirm.', 'Der Hund ist im Garten.', 'Ich liebe Kaffee.']),
 'it': ('Gli articoli: a, an, the', "«A» davanti a un suono consonantico (a book, a university), «an» davanti a un suono vocalico (an apple, an hour). Significano «un, una» e si usano solo al singolare.\n«The» (il, la, i, le) non cambia mai. Si usa per ciò che è noto o già menzionato.\nNiente articolo per parlare in generale: I like music. Dogs are friendly.", ['Ho un cane e un ombrello.', 'Il cane è in giardino.', 'Adoro il caffè.']),
 'pt': ('Os artigos: a, an, the', "«A» antes de som de consoante (a book, a university), «an» antes de som de vogal (an apple, an hour). Significam «um, uma» e só se usam no singular.\n«The» (o, a, os, as) nunca muda. Usa-se para o que é conhecido ou já mencionado.\nSem artigo para falar em geral: I like music. Dogs are friendly.", ['Tenho um cachorro e um guarda-chuva.', 'O cachorro está no jardim.', 'Adoro café.']),
 'ja': ('冠詞：a, an, the', "子音の音の前は「a」（a book, a university）、母音の音の前は「an」（an apple, an hour）。「一つの」という意味で、単数にだけ使います。\n「the」は形が変わりません。すでに知っているもの、話に出たものに使います。\n一般的なことを言うときは冠詞をつけません：I like music. Dogs are friendly.", ['犬を一匹と傘を一本持っています。', 'その犬は庭にいます。', 'コーヒーが大好きです。']),
 'zh': ('冠词：a、an、the', "辅音音素前用「a」（a book, a university），元音音素前用「an」（an apple, an hour）。意思是「一个」，只用于单数。\n「the」（这个、那个）形式不变，用于已知或已提到的事物。\n泛指时不用冠词：I like music. Dogs are friendly.", ['我有一只狗和一把伞。', '那只狗在花园里。', '我很喜欢咖啡。']),
 'ko': ('관사: a, an, the', "자음 소리 앞에는 「a」(a book, a university), 모음 소리 앞에는 「an」(an apple, an hour)을 씁니다. '하나의'라는 뜻이며 단수에만 씁니다.\n「the」는 형태가 바뀌지 않습니다. 이미 알거나 앞에서 말한 것에 씁니다.\n일반적인 이야기를 할 때는 관사를 쓰지 않습니다: I like music. Dogs are friendly.", ['저는 개 한 마리와 우산 하나가 있어요.', '그 개는 정원에 있어요.', '저는 커피를 정말 좋아해요.']),
 'lt': ('Artikeliai: a, an, the', "„A“ prieš priebalsio garsą (a book, a university), „an“ prieš balsio garsą (an apple, an hour). Jie reiškia „vienas, kažkoks“ ir vartojami tik vienaskaitoje.\n„The“ niekada nekinta. Jis vartojamas tam, kas žinoma ar jau paminėta.\nKalbant apskritai artikelio nėra: I like music. Dogs are friendly.", ['Turiu šunį ir skėtį.', 'Šuo yra sode.', 'Aš labai mėgstu kavą.']),
 'tl': ('Mga pantukoy: a, an, the', "«A» bago ang tunog-katinig (a book, a university), «an» bago ang tunog-patinig (an apple, an hour). Ibig sabihin ay «isang» at pang-isahan lamang.\nHindi nagbabago ang «the». Ginagamit ito sa kilala o nabanggit na.\nWalang pantukoy kapag pangkalahatan: I like music. Dogs are friendly.", ['May aso ako at isang payong.', 'Nasa hardin ang aso.', 'Gustong-gusto ko ang kape.']),
},
'plural': {
 'es': ('El plural de los sustantivos', "Se añade -s: book → books. Tras -s, -x, -ch, -sh se añade -es: box → boxes. Consonante + y → -ies: city → cities. -f / -fe → -ves: knife → knives.\nAlgunos plurales irregulares: man → men, woman → women, child → children, foot → feet, tooth → teeth, person → people.\nEl adjetivo nunca lleva -s: two big houses.", ['Dos niños están jugando.', 'Compré tres cajas.']),
 'de': ('Der Plural der Nomen', "Man hängt -s an: book → books. Nach -s, -x, -ch, -sh kommt -es: box → boxes. Konsonant + y → -ies: city → cities. -f / -fe → -ves: knife → knives.\nEinige unregelmäßige Plurale: man → men, woman → women, child → children, foot → feet, tooth → teeth, person → people.\nDas Adjektiv bekommt nie ein -s: two big houses.", ['Zwei Kinder spielen.', 'Ich habe drei Kisten gekauft.']),
 'it': ('Il plurale dei nomi', "Si aggiunge -s: book → books. Dopo -s, -x, -ch, -sh si aggiunge -es: box → boxes. Consonante + y → -ies: city → cities. -f / -fe → -ves: knife → knives.\nAlcuni plurali irregolari: man → men, woman → women, child → children, foot → feet, tooth → teeth, person → people.\nL'aggettivo non prende mai la -s: two big houses.", ['Due bambini stanno giocando.', 'Ho comprato tre scatole.']),
 'pt': ('O plural dos substantivos', "Acrescenta-se -s: book → books. Depois de -s, -x, -ch, -sh acrescenta-se -es: box → boxes. Consoante + y → -ies: city → cities. -f / -fe → -ves: knife → knives.\nAlguns plurais irregulares: man → men, woman → women, child → children, foot → feet, tooth → teeth, person → people.\nO adjetivo nunca leva -s: two big houses.", ['Duas crianças estão brincando.', 'Comprei três caixas.']),
 'ja': ('名詞の複数形', "-s をつけます：book → books。-s, -x, -ch, -sh で終わる語は -es：box → boxes。子音 + y は -ies：city → cities。-f / -fe は -ves：knife → knives。\n不規則な複数形：man → men, woman → women, child → children, foot → feet, tooth → teeth, person → people。\n形容詞には -s をつけません：two big houses。", ['子供が二人遊んでいます。', '箱を三つ買いました。']),
 'zh': ('名词的复数', "一般加 -s：book → books。以 -s, -x, -ch, -sh 结尾加 -es：box → boxes。辅音 + y 变 -ies：city → cities。-f / -fe 变 -ves：knife → knives。\n一些不规则复数：man → men，woman → women，child → children，foot → feet，tooth → teeth，person → people。\n形容词永远不加 -s：two big houses。", ['两个孩子在玩。', '我买了三个盒子。']),
 'ko': ('명사의 복수형', "-s를 붙입니다: book → books. -s, -x, -ch, -sh 뒤에는 -es: box → boxes. 자음 + y는 -ies: city → cities. -f / -fe는 -ves: knife → knives.\n불규칙 복수형: man → men, woman → women, child → children, foot → feet, tooth → teeth, person → people.\n형용사에는 절대 -s를 붙이지 않습니다: two big houses.", ['아이 둘이 놀고 있어요.', '상자를 세 개 샀어요.']),
 'lt': ('Daiktavardžių daugiskaita', "Pridedama -s: book → books. Po -s, -x, -ch, -sh pridedama -es: box → boxes. Priebalsis + y → -ies: city → cities. -f / -fe → -ves: knife → knives.\nKai kurios netaisyklingos daugiskaitos: man → men, woman → women, child → children, foot → feet, tooth → teeth, person → people.\nBūdvardis niekada negauna -s: two big houses.", ['Du vaikai žaidžia.', 'Nusipirkau tris dėžes.']),
 'tl': ('Ang maramihan ng pangngalan', "Idagdag ang -s: book → books. Pagkatapos ng -s, -x, -ch, -sh, idagdag ang -es: box → boxes. Katinig + y → -ies: city → cities. -f / -fe → -ves: knife → knives.\nIlang di-regular: man → men, woman → women, child → children, foot → feet, tooth → teeth, person → people.\nHindi kailanman nagkakaroon ng -s ang pang-uri: two big houses.", ['Dalawang bata ang naglalaro.', 'Bumili ako ng tatlong kahon.']),
},
'present-simple': {
 'es': ('El presente simple', "Expresa hábitos y hechos generales. El verbo solo cambia en la tercera persona del singular, que lleva -s: I work, she works (go → goes, study → studies, have → has).\nNegación con do / does + not: I don't work, she doesn't work (el verbo pierde la -s).\nPregunta: Do you work? Does she work?", ['Él trabaja en un banco.', 'No hablo chino.', '¿Vive ella aquí?']),
 'de': ('Das Simple Present', "Es drückt Gewohnheiten und allgemeine Tatsachen aus. Das Verb ändert sich nur in der 3. Person Singular, die ein -s bekommt: I work, she works (go → goes, study → studies, have → has).\nVerneinung mit do / does + not: I don't work, she doesn't work (das Verb verliert sein -s).\nFrage: Do you work? Does she work?", ['Er arbeitet in einer Bank.', 'Ich spreche kein Chinesisch.', 'Wohnt sie hier?']),
 'it': ('Il present simple', "Esprime abitudini e fatti generali. Il verbo cambia solo alla terza persona singolare, che prende -s: I work, she works (go → goes, study → studies, have → has).\nNegazione con do / does + not: I don't work, she doesn't work (il verbo perde la -s).\nDomanda: Do you work? Does she work?", ['Lavora in una banca.', 'Non parlo cinese.', 'Lei abita qui?']),
 'pt': ('O present simple', "Expressa hábitos e fatos gerais. O verbo só muda na terceira pessoa do singular, que leva -s: I work, she works (go → goes, study → studies, have → has).\nNegação com do / does + not: I don't work, she doesn't work (o verbo perde o -s).\nPergunta: Do you work? Does she work?", ['Ele trabalha num banco.', 'Não falo chinês.', 'Ela mora aqui?']),
 'ja': ('現在形', "習慣や一般的な事実を表します。動詞が変わるのは三人称単数だけで、-s がつきます：I work, she works（go → goes, study → studies, have → has）。\n否定は do / does + not：I don't work, she doesn't work（動詞の -s はなくなります）。\n疑問文：Do you work? Does she work?", ['彼は銀行で働いています。', '中国語は話せません。', '彼女はここに住んでいますか？']),
 'zh': ('一般现在时', "表示习惯和一般事实。动词只在第三人称单数时变化，加 -s：I work，she works（go → goes，study → studies，have → has）。\n否定用 do / does + not：I don't work，she doesn't work（动词去掉 -s）。\n疑问：Do you work? Does she work?", ['他在银行工作。', '我不会说中文。', '她住在这里吗？']),
 'ko': ('현재 시제', "습관이나 일반적인 사실을 나타냅니다. 동사는 3인칭 단수일 때만 바뀌며 -s가 붙습니다: I work, she works (go → goes, study → studies, have → has).\n부정은 do / does + not: I don't work, she doesn't work (동사의 -s가 없어집니다).\n의문문: Do you work? Does she work?", ['그는 은행에서 일해요.', '저는 중국어를 못해요.', '그녀는 여기 살아요?']),
 'lt': ('Paprastasis esamasis laikas', "Jis reiškia įpročius ir bendrus faktus. Veiksmažodis keičiasi tik vienaskaitos trečiajame asmenyje, kur pridedamas -s: I work, she works (go → goes, study → studies, have → has).\nNeiginys su do / does + not: I don't work, she doesn't work (veiksmažodis netenka -s).\nKlausimas: Do you work? Does she work?", ['Jis dirba banke.', 'Aš nekalbu kiniškai.', 'Ar ji čia gyvena?']),
 'tl': ('Ang simple present', "Nagpapahayag ito ng gawi at pangkalahatang katotohanan. Nagbabago lang ang pandiwa sa ikatlong panauhan isahan, na may -s: I work, she works (go → goes, study → studies, have → has).\nNegatibo gamit ang do / does + not: I don't work, she doesn't work (nawawala ang -s).\nTanong: Do you work? Does she work?", ['Nagtatrabaho siya sa bangko.', 'Hindi ako marunong mag-Intsik.', 'Dito ba siya nakatira?']),
},
'possessives': {
 'es': ('Pronombres y posesivos', "Sujeto: I, you, he, she, it, we, they. Complemento: me, you, him, her, it, us, them.\nPosesivos: my, your, his, her, its, our, their. Concuerdan con el poseedor, no con lo poseído: his sister = la hermana de él, her brother = el hermano de ella.\nPosesión con 's: Tom's car (el coche de Tom).", ['Este es mi hermano y su esposa.', 'Dáselo a ellos.']),
 'de': ('Pronomen und Possessivbegleiter', "Subjekt: I, you, he, she, it, we, they. Objekt: me, you, him, her, it, us, them.\nPossessiv: my, your, his, her, its, our, their. Sie richten sich nach dem Besitzer, nicht nach dem Besitz: his sister = seine Schwester, her brother = ihr Bruder.\nBesitz mit 's: Tom's car (Toms Auto).", ['Das ist mein Bruder und seine Frau.', 'Gib es ihnen.']),
 'it': ('Pronomi e possessivi', "Soggetto: I, you, he, she, it, we, they. Complemento: me, you, him, her, it, us, them.\nPossessivi: my, your, his, her, its, our, their. Si accordano con il possessore, non con la cosa posseduta: his sister = la sorella di lui, her brother = il fratello di lei.\nPossesso con 's: Tom's car (la macchina di Tom).", ['Questo è mio fratello e sua moglie.', 'Daglielo.']),
 'pt': ('Pronomes e possessivos', "Sujeito: I, you, he, she, it, we, they. Complemento: me, you, him, her, it, us, them.\nPossessivos: my, your, his, her, its, our, their. Concordam com o possuidor, não com a coisa possuída: his sister = a irmã dele, her brother = o irmão dela.\nPosse com 's: Tom's car (o carro do Tom).", ['Este é meu irmão e a esposa dele.', 'Dê isso a eles.']),
 'ja': ('代名詞と所有格', "主格：I, you, he, she, it, we, they。目的格：me, you, him, her, it, us, them。\n所有格：my, your, his, her, its, our, their。持ち主に合わせ、持ち物には合わせません：his sister = 彼の姉妹、her brother = 彼女の兄弟。\n's で所有を表します：Tom's car（トムの車）。", ['こちらは私の兄と彼の妻です。', 'それを彼らに渡して。']),
 'zh': ('代词与物主代词', "主格：I, you, he, she, it, we, they。宾格：me, you, him, her, it, us, them。\n物主代词：my, your, his, her, its, our, their。随所有者变化，而不是随所属物：his sister = 他的姐妹，her brother = 她的兄弟。\n用 's 表示所属：Tom's car（汤姆的车）。", ['这是我哥哥和他的妻子。', '把它给他们。']),
 'ko': ('대명사와 소유격', "주격: I, you, he, she, it, we, they. 목적격: me, you, him, her, it, us, them.\n소유격: my, your, his, her, its, our, their. 소유한 물건이 아니라 소유자에 맞춥니다: his sister = 그의 누나, her brother = 그녀의 남동생.\n's로 소유를 나타냅니다: Tom's car (톰의 차).", ['이쪽은 제 형과 형의 아내예요.', '그걸 그들에게 줘.']),
 'lt': ('Įvardžiai ir savybiniai žodžiai', "Veiksnys: I, you, he, she, it, we, they. Papildinys: me, you, him, her, it, us, them.\nSavybiniai: my, your, his, her, its, our, their. Jie derinami su savininku, o ne su daiktu: his sister = jo sesuo, her brother = jos brolis.\nPriklausomybė su 's: Tom's car (Tomo automobilis).", ['Tai mano brolis ir jo žmona.', 'Duok tai jiems.']),
 'tl': ('Panghalip at paari', "Simuno: I, you, he, she, it, we, they. Layon: me, you, him, her, it, us, them.\nPaari: my, your, his, her, its, our, their. Sumusunod sa may-ari, hindi sa inaari: his sister = kapatid niyang babae (lalaki ang may-ari), her brother = kapatid niyang lalaki (babae ang may-ari).\nPag-aari gamit ang 's: Tom's car (kotse ni Tom).", ['Ito ang kuya ko at ang asawa niya.', 'Ibigay mo iyan sa kanila.']),
},
'there-is': {
 'es': ('There is, there are', "«There is» + singular, «there are» + plural: hay. Negación: there isn't / there aren't. Pregunta: Is there…? Are there…?\nEn pasado: there was / there were.", ['Hay un gato en el tejado.', '¿Hay preguntas?']),
 'de': ('There is, there are', "„There is“ + Singular, „there are“ + Plural: es gibt. Verneinung: there isn't / there aren't. Frage: Is there…? Are there…?\nVergangenheit: there was / there were.", ['Auf dem Dach ist eine Katze.', 'Gibt es Fragen?']),
 'it': ('There is, there are', "«There is» + singolare, «there are» + plurale: c'è, ci sono. Negazione: there isn't / there aren't. Domanda: Is there…? Are there…?\nAl passato: there was / there were.", ["C'è un gatto sul tetto.", 'Ci sono domande?']),
 'pt': ('There is, there are', "«There is» + singular, «there are» + plural: há. Negação: there isn't / there aren't. Pergunta: Is there…? Are there…?\nNo passado: there was / there were.", ['Há um gato no telhado.', 'Há alguma pergunta?']),
 'ja': ('There is / there are（〜がある）', "単数は「there is」、複数は「there are」：〜があります、〜がいます。否定：there isn't / there aren't。疑問：Is there…? Are there…?\n過去形：there was / there were。", ['屋根の上に猫がいます。', '質問はありますか？']),
 'zh': ('There is / there are（有）', "单数用「there is」，复数用「there are」：有……。否定：there isn't / there aren't。疑问：Is there…? Are there…?\n过去时：there was / there were。", ['屋顶上有一只猫。', '有问题吗？']),
 'ko': ('There is / there are (~이 있다)', "단수에는 「there is」, 복수에는 「there are」: ~이 있다. 부정: there isn't / there aren't. 의문: Is there…? Are there…?\n과거: there was / there were.", ['지붕 위에 고양이가 있어요.', '질문 있어요?']),
 'lt': ('There is, there are (yra)', "„There is“ + vienaskaita, „there are“ + daugiskaita: yra. Neiginys: there isn't / there aren't. Klausimas: Is there…? Are there…?\nBūtuoju laiku: there was / there were.", ['Ant stogo yra katė.', 'Ar yra klausimų?']),
 'tl': ('There is, there are (may)', "«There is» + isahan, «there are» + maramihan: may, mayroon. Negatibo: there isn't / there aren't. Tanong: Is there…? Are there…?\nNakaraan: there was / there were.", ['May pusa sa bubong.', 'May tanong ba?']),
},
'can': {
 'es': ('Can: poder, saber hacer', "«Can» va seguido del verbo sin «to» y nunca lleva -s: she can swim. Negación: cannot / can't. Pregunta: Can you help me?\nPasado: could.", ['Sé hablar inglés.', 'Ella no puede venir hoy.']),
 'de': ('Can: können', "Nach „can“ folgt das Verb ohne „to“; „can“ bekommt nie ein -s: she can swim. Verneinung: cannot / can't. Frage: Can you help me?\nVergangenheit: could.", ['Ich kann Englisch sprechen.', 'Sie kann heute nicht kommen.']),
 'it': ('Can: potere, saper fare', "«Can» è seguito dal verbo senza «to» e non prende mai la -s: she can swim. Negazione: cannot / can't. Domanda: Can you help me?\nPassato: could.", ["So parlare inglese.", 'Oggi non può venire.']),
 'pt': ('Can: poder, saber fazer', "«Can» é seguido do verbo sem «to» e nunca leva -s: she can swim. Negação: cannot / can't. Pergunta: Can you help me?\nPassado: could.", ['Eu sei falar inglês.', 'Ela não pode vir hoje.']),
 'ja': ('can：できる', "can の後ろには to のない動詞が来て、can には -s がつきません：she can swim。否定：cannot / can't。疑問：Can you help me?\n過去形：could。", ['私は英語が話せます。', '彼女は今日来られません。']),
 'zh': ('can：能、会', "can 后接不带 to 的动词，can 本身从不加 -s：she can swim。否定：cannot / can't。疑问：Can you help me?\n过去式：could。", ['我会说英语。', '她今天不能来。']),
 'ko': ('can: ~할 수 있다', "can 뒤에는 to 없는 동사가 오고, can에는 절대 -s가 붙지 않습니다: she can swim. 부정: cannot / can't. 의문: Can you help me?\n과거: could.", ['저는 영어를 할 줄 알아요.', '그녀는 오늘 올 수 없어요.']),
 'lt': ('Can: galėti, mokėti', "Po „can“ eina veiksmažodis be „to“, o „can“ niekada negauna -s: she can swim. Neiginys: cannot / can't. Klausimas: Can you help me?\nBūtasis laikas: could.", ['Aš moku kalbėti angliškai.', 'Ji šiandien negali ateiti.']),
 'tl': ('Can: kaya, marunong', "Sinusundan ang «can» ng pandiwang walang «to» at hindi kailanman nagkakaroon ng -s: she can swim. Negatibo: cannot / can't. Tanong: Can you help me?\nNakaraan: could.", ['Marunong akong mag-Ingles.', 'Hindi siya makakapunta ngayon.']),
},
'prepositions': {
 'es': ('Preposiciones: in, on, at', "Lugar: «in» dentro de un espacio (in the kitchen, in France), «on» sobre una superficie (on the table), «at» en un punto preciso (at the station, at home).\nTiempo: «in» para meses, años, estaciones (in May, in 2020), «on» para días y fechas (on Monday), «at» para horas (at six o'clock) y at night.", ['Las llaves están en la mesa.', 'Nací en julio.', 'Nos vemos a las cinco.']),
 'de': ('Präpositionen: in, on, at', "Ort: „in“ innerhalb eines Raums (in the kitchen, in France), „on“ auf einer Fläche (on the table), „at“ an einem bestimmten Punkt (at the station, at home).\nZeit: „in“ für Monate, Jahre, Jahreszeiten (in May, in 2020), „on“ für Tage und Daten (on Monday), „at“ für Uhrzeiten (at six o'clock) und at night.", ['Die Schlüssel liegen auf dem Tisch.', 'Ich bin im Juli geboren.', 'Bis um fünf.']),
 'it': ('Preposizioni: in, on, at', "Luogo: «in» dentro uno spazio (in the kitchen, in France), «on» su una superficie (on the table), «at» in un punto preciso (at the station, at home).\nTempo: «in» per mesi, anni, stagioni (in May, in 2020), «on» per giorni e date (on Monday), «at» per le ore (at six o'clock) e at night.", ['Le chiavi sono sul tavolo.', 'Sono nato a luglio.', 'Ci vediamo alle cinque.']),
 'pt': ('Preposições: in, on, at', "Lugar: «in» dentro de um espaço (in the kitchen, in France), «on» sobre uma superfície (on the table), «at» num ponto preciso (at the station, at home).\nTempo: «in» para meses, anos, estações (in May, in 2020), «on» para dias e datas (on Monday), «at» para horas (at six o'clock) e at night.", ['As chaves estão na mesa.', 'Nasci em julho.', 'Até as cinco.']),
 'ja': ('前置詞 in, on, at', "場所：「in」は空間の中（in the kitchen, in France）、「on」は面の上（on the table）、「at」は特定の地点（at the station, at home）。\n時：「in」は月・年・季節（in May, in 2020）、「on」は曜日・日付（on Monday）、「at」は時刻（at six o'clock）と at night。", ['鍵はテーブルの上にあります。', '私は7月生まれです。', '5時に会いましょう。']),
 'zh': ('介词 in、on、at', "地点：「in」表示在空间内（in the kitchen, in France），「on」表示在表面上（on the table），「at」表示在某个点（at the station, at home）。\n时间：「in」用于月、年、季节（in May, in 2020），「on」用于日子和日期（on Monday），「at」用于钟点（at six o'clock）和 at night。", ['钥匙在桌子上。', '我是七月出生的。', '五点见。']),
 'ko': ('전치사 in, on, at', "장소: 「in」은 공간 안(in the kitchen, in France), 「on」은 표면 위(on the table), 「at」은 특정 지점(at the station, at home).\n시간: 「in」은 월, 연도, 계절(in May, in 2020), 「on」은 요일과 날짜(on Monday), 「at」은 시각(at six o'clock)과 at night.", ['열쇠는 탁자 위에 있어요.', '저는 7월에 태어났어요.', '다섯 시에 봐요.']),
 'lt': ('Prielinksniai in, on, at', "Vieta: „in“ – erdvės viduje (in the kitchen, in France), „on“ – ant paviršiaus (on the table), „at“ – tam tikrame taške (at the station, at home).\nLaikas: „in“ mėnesiams, metams, metų laikams (in May, in 2020), „on“ dienoms ir datoms (on Monday), „at“ valandoms (at six o'clock) ir at night.", ['Raktai ant stalo.', 'Gimiau liepą.', 'Iki penktos.']),
 'tl': ('Pang-ukol: in, on, at', "Lugar: «in» sa loob ng espasyo (in the kitchen, in France), «on» sa ibabaw (on the table), «at» sa tiyak na punto (at the station, at home).\nOras: «in» para sa buwan, taon, panahon (in May, in 2020), «on» para sa araw at petsa (on Monday), «at» para sa oras (at six o'clock) at at night.", ['Nasa mesa ang mga susi.', 'Ipinanganak ako noong Hulyo.', 'Kita tayo nang alas-singko.']),
},
'present-continuous': {
 'es': ('El presente continuo', "be + verbo en -ing: acción en curso en el momento en que se habla. I am reading, she is sleeping, they are working.\nOrtografía: make → making, run → running.\nTambién sirve para un plan cercano: I'm leaving tomorrow.\nLos verbos de estado (know, like, want, need) no se usan en esta forma.", ['¿Qué estás haciendo?', 'Está lloviendo.']),
 'de': ('Das Present Continuous', "be + Verb mit -ing: Handlung, die gerade abläuft. I am reading, she is sleeping, they are working.\nSchreibung: make → making, run → running.\nAuch für nahe Pläne: I'm leaving tomorrow.\nZustandsverben (know, like, want, need) stehen nicht in dieser Form.", ['Was machst du gerade?', 'Es regnet.']),
 'it': ('Il present continuous', "be + verbo in -ing: azione in corso mentre si parla. I am reading, she is sleeping, they are working.\nOrtografia: make → making, run → running.\nServe anche per un programma vicino: I'm leaving tomorrow.\nI verbi di stato (know, like, want, need) non si usano in questa forma.", ['Che cosa stai facendo?', 'Sta piovendo.']),
 'pt': ('O present continuous', "be + verbo em -ing: ação em curso no momento em que se fala. I am reading, she is sleeping, they are working.\nOrtografia: make → making, run → running.\nServe também para planos próximos: I'm leaving tomorrow.\nVerbos de estado (know, like, want, need) não se usam nesta forma.", ['O que você está fazendo?', 'Está chovendo.']),
 'ja': ('現在進行形', "be + 動詞の -ing 形：話している今、進行中の動作。I am reading, she is sleeping, they are working。\nつづり：make → making, run → running。\n近い予定にも使います：I'm leaving tomorrow。\n状態を表す動詞（know, like, want, need）はこの形にしません。", ['何をしているの？', '雨が降っています。']),
 'zh': ('现在进行时', "be + 动词 -ing：说话时正在进行的动作。I am reading，she is sleeping，they are working。\n拼写：make → making，run → running。\n也可表示近期计划：I'm leaving tomorrow。\n状态动词（know, like, want, need）不用这种形式。", ['你在做什么？', '在下雨。']),
 'ko': ('현재 진행형', "be + 동사 -ing: 말하는 지금 진행 중인 동작. I am reading, she is sleeping, they are working.\n철자: make → making, run → running.\n가까운 예정에도 씁니다: I'm leaving tomorrow.\n상태 동사(know, like, want, need)는 이 형태로 쓰지 않습니다.", ['뭐 하고 있어요?', '비가 오고 있어요.']),
 'lt': ('Esamasis eigos laikas', "be + veiksmažodis su -ing: veiksmas, vykstantis kalbant. I am reading, she is sleeping, they are working.\nRašyba: make → making, run → running.\nVartojamas ir artimiems planams: I'm leaving tomorrow.\nBūsenos veiksmažodžiai (know, like, want, need) šia forma nevartojami.", ['Ką tu darai?', 'Lyja.']),
 'tl': ('Ang present continuous', "be + pandiwang may -ing: kilos na nangyayari habang nagsasalita. I am reading, she is sleeping, they are working.\nBaybay: make → making, run → running.\nGinagamit din para sa malapit na plano: I'm leaving tomorrow.\nHindi ginagamit sa ganitong anyo ang mga pandiwa ng kalagayan (know, like, want, need).", ['Ano ang ginagawa mo?', 'Umuulan.']),
},
'past-simple': {
 'es': ('El pasado simple (past simple)', "Acción terminada en el pasado. Verbos regulares: + -ed (worked, played, studied). Muchos verbos frecuentes son irregulares: go → went, have → had, see → saw, do → did, take → took, come → came.\n«Be»: was (I, he, she, it), were (you, we, they).\nNegación y pregunta con did: I didn't go. Did you see it? (el verbo queda en su forma base).", ['Fui a Londres el año pasado.', 'Ella no me llamó.']),
 'de': ('Das Simple Past', "Abgeschlossene Handlung in der Vergangenheit. Regelmäßige Verben: + -ed (worked, played, studied). Viele häufige Verben sind unregelmäßig: go → went, have → had, see → saw, do → did, take → took, come → came.\n„Be“: was (I, he, she, it), were (you, we, they).\nVerneinung und Frage mit did: I didn't go. Did you see it? (das Verb bleibt in der Grundform).", ['Letztes Jahr bin ich nach London gefahren.', 'Sie hat mich nicht angerufen.']),
 'it': ('Il passato semplice (past simple)', "Azione conclusa nel passato. Verbi regolari: + -ed (worked, played, studied). Molti verbi frequenti sono irregolari: go → went, have → had, see → saw, do → did, take → took, come → came.\n«Be»: was (I, he, she, it), were (you, we, they).\nNegazione e domanda con did: I didn't go. Did you see it? (il verbo resta alla forma base).", ["L'anno scorso sono andato a Londra.", 'Non mi ha chiamato.']),
 'pt': ('O passado simples (past simple)', "Ação terminada no passado. Verbos regulares: + -ed (worked, played, studied). Muitos verbos comuns são irregulares: go → went, have → had, see → saw, do → did, take → took, come → came.\n«Be»: was (I, he, she, it), were (you, we, they).\nNegação e pergunta com did: I didn't go. Did you see it? (o verbo fica na forma base).", ['Fui a Londres no ano passado.', 'Ela não me ligou.']),
 'ja': ('過去形', "過去に終わった動作。規則動詞は -ed をつけます（worked, played, studied）。よく使う動詞の多くは不規則です：go → went, have → had, see → saw, do → did, take → took, come → came。\nbe 動詞：was（I, he, she, it）、were（you, we, they）。\n否定と疑問は did を使います：I didn't go. Did you see it?（動詞は原形のまま）。", ['去年ロンドンへ行きました。', '彼女は電話をくれませんでした。']),
 'zh': ('一般过去时', "过去已结束的动作。规则动词加 -ed（worked, played, studied）。许多常用动词不规则：go → went，have → had，see → saw，do → did，take → took，come → came。\nbe：was（I, he, she, it），were（you, we, they）。\n否定和疑问用 did：I didn't go. Did you see it?（动词用原形）。", ['我去年去了伦敦。', '她没给我打电话。']),
 'ko': ('과거 시제', "과거에 끝난 동작. 규칙 동사는 -ed를 붙입니다(worked, played, studied). 자주 쓰는 동사 중 다수가 불규칙입니다: go → went, have → had, see → saw, do → did, take → took, come → came.\nbe 동사: was(I, he, she, it), were(you, we, they).\n부정과 의문은 did로 만듭니다: I didn't go. Did you see it? (동사는 원형).", ['작년에 런던에 갔어요.', '그녀는 저에게 전화하지 않았어요.']),
 'lt': ('Paprastasis būtasis laikas', "Praeityje pasibaigęs veiksmas. Taisyklingi veiksmažodžiai: + -ed (worked, played, studied). Daug dažnų veiksmažodžių netaisyklingi: go → went, have → had, see → saw, do → did, take → took, come → came.\n„Be“: was (I, he, she, it), were (you, we, they).\nNeiginys ir klausimas su did: I didn't go. Did you see it? (veiksmažodis lieka pagrindinės formos).", ['Pernai buvau Londone.', 'Ji man nepaskambino.']),
 'tl': ('Ang past simple', "Tapos na kilos sa nakaraan. Regular na pandiwa: + -ed (worked, played, studied). Maraming karaniwang pandiwa ang di-regular: go → went, have → had, see → saw, do → did, take → took, come → came.\n«Be»: was (I, he, she, it), were (you, we, they).\nNegatibo at tanong gamit ang did: I didn't go. Did you see it? (nananatili sa batayang anyo ang pandiwa).", ['Pumunta ako sa London noong isang taon.', 'Hindi niya ako tinawagan.']),
},
'future': {
 'es': ('El futuro: will y be going to', "«Will» + verbo: decisión tomada en el momento, predicción, promesa (I'll help you). Negación: won't.\n«Be going to» + verbo: intención ya decidida o algo que se ve venir (I'm going to buy a car. It's going to rain).", ['Te llamaré mañana.', 'Nos vamos a mudar.']),
 'de': ('Die Zukunft: will und be going to', "„Will“ + Verb: spontane Entscheidung, Vorhersage, Versprechen (I'll help you). Verneinung: won't.\n„Be going to“ + Verb: bereits gefasste Absicht oder etwas, das man kommen sieht (I'm going to buy a car. It's going to rain).", ['Ich rufe dich morgen an.', 'Wir werden umziehen.']),
 'it': ('Il futuro: will e be going to', "«Will» + verbo: decisione presa sul momento, previsione, promessa (I'll help you). Negazione: won't.\n«Be going to» + verbo: intenzione già decisa o qualcosa che si vede arrivare (I'm going to buy a car. It's going to rain).", ['Ti chiamerò domani.', 'Stiamo per traslocare.']),
 'pt': ('O futuro: will e be going to', "«Will» + verbo: decisão tomada na hora, previsão, promessa (I'll help you). Negação: won't.\n«Be going to» + verbo: intenção já decidida ou algo que se vê chegar (I'm going to buy a car. It's going to rain).", ['Eu te ligo amanhã.', 'Vamos nos mudar.']),
 'ja': ('未来：will と be going to', "will + 動詞：その場の決定、予測、約束（I'll help you）。否定：won't。\nbe going to + 動詞：すでに決めた予定、兆しのあること（I'm going to buy a car. It's going to rain）。", ['明日電話します。', '私たちは引っ越す予定です。']),
 'zh': ('将来时：will 与 be going to', "will + 动词：当场做的决定、预测、承诺（I'll help you）。否定：won't。\nbe going to + 动词：已经决定的打算，或有迹象将要发生的事（I'm going to buy a car. It's going to rain）。", ['我明天给你打电话。', '我们要搬家了。']),
 'ko': ('미래: will과 be going to', "will + 동사: 그 자리에서 내린 결정, 예측, 약속(I'll help you). 부정: won't.\nbe going to + 동사: 이미 정한 계획이나 곧 일어날 것이 보이는 일(I'm going to buy a car. It's going to rain).", ['내일 전화할게요.', '우리는 이사할 거예요.']),
 'lt': ('Būsimasis laikas: will ir be going to', "„Will“ + veiksmažodis: tuo metu priimtas sprendimas, spėjimas, pažadas (I'll help you). Neiginys: won't.\n„Be going to“ + veiksmažodis: jau nuspręstas ketinimas arba tai, kas akivaizdžiai artėja (I'm going to buy a car. It's going to rain).", ['Paskambinsiu tau rytoj.', 'Mes ketiname persikraustyti.']),
 'tl': ('Ang hinaharap: will at be going to', "«Will» + pandiwa: pasyang ginawa sa sandaling iyon, hula, pangako (I'll help you). Negatibo: won't.\n«Be going to» + pandiwa: balak na napagpasyahan na o bagay na halatang darating (I'm going to buy a car. It's going to rain).", ['Tatawagan kita bukas.', 'Lilipat kami ng bahay.']),
},
'comparatives': {
 'es': ('Comparativo y superlativo', "Adjetivos cortos: -er … than, the -est (tall → taller than, the tallest; big → bigger; happy → happier).\nAdjetivos largos: more … than, the most … (more expensive, the most beautiful).\nIrregulares: good → better → the best; bad → worse → the worst; far → farther.\nIgualdad: as … as (as tall as).", ['Ella es mayor que yo.', 'Es la mejor película del año.']),
 'de': ('Komparativ und Superlativ', "Kurze Adjektive: -er … than, the -est (tall → taller than, the tallest; big → bigger; happy → happier).\nLange Adjektive: more … than, the most … (more expensive, the most beautiful).\nUnregelmäßig: good → better → the best; bad → worse → the worst; far → farther.\nGleichheit: as … as (as tall as).", ['Sie ist älter als ich.', 'Das ist der beste Film des Jahres.']),
 'it': ('Comparativo e superlativo', "Aggettivi brevi: -er … than, the -est (tall → taller than, the tallest; big → bigger; happy → happier).\nAggettivi lunghi: more … than, the most … (more expensive, the most beautiful).\nIrregolari: good → better → the best; bad → worse → the worst; far → farther.\nUguaglianza: as … as (as tall as).", ['Lei è più grande di me.', "È il miglior film dell'anno."]),
 'pt': ('Comparativo e superlativo', "Adjetivos curtos: -er … than, the -est (tall → taller than, the tallest; big → bigger; happy → happier).\nAdjetivos longos: more … than, the most … (more expensive, the most beautiful).\nIrregulares: good → better → the best; bad → worse → the worst; far → farther.\nIgualdade: as … as (as tall as).", ['Ela é mais velha do que eu.', 'É o melhor filme do ano.']),
 'ja': ('比較級と最上級', "短い形容詞：-er … than、the -est（tall → taller than, the tallest; big → bigger; happy → happier）。\n長い形容詞：more … than、the most …（more expensive, the most beautiful）。\n不規則：good → better → the best、bad → worse → the worst、far → farther。\n同等：as … as（as tall as）。", ['彼女は私より年上です。', '今年一番の映画です。']),
 'zh': ('比较级和最高级', "短形容词：-er … than，the -est（tall → taller than, the tallest；big → bigger；happy → happier）。\n长形容词：more … than，the most …（more expensive, the most beautiful）。\n不规则：good → better → the best；bad → worse → the worst；far → farther。\n同级：as … as（as tall as）。", ['她比我大。', '这是今年最好的电影。']),
 'ko': ('비교급과 최상급', "짧은 형용사: -er … than, the -est (tall → taller than, the tallest; big → bigger; happy → happier).\n긴 형용사: more … than, the most … (more expensive, the most beautiful).\n불규칙: good → better → the best; bad → worse → the worst; far → farther.\n동등: as … as (as tall as).", ['그녀는 저보다 나이가 많아요.', '올해 최고의 영화예요.']),
 'lt': ('Aukštesnysis ir aukščiausiasis laipsnis', "Trumpi būdvardžiai: -er … than, the -est (tall → taller than, the tallest; big → bigger; happy → happier).\nIlgi būdvardžiai: more … than, the most … (more expensive, the most beautiful).\nNetaisyklingi: good → better → the best; bad → worse → the worst; far → farther.\nLygybė: as … as (as tall as).", ['Ji vyresnė už mane.', 'Tai geriausias metų filmas.']),
 'tl': ('Paghahambing', "Maiikling pang-uri: -er … than, the -est (tall → taller than, the tallest; big → bigger; happy → happier).\nMahahabang pang-uri: more … than, the most … (more expensive, the most beautiful).\nDi-regular: good → better → the best; bad → worse → the worst; far → farther.\nPagkakapantay: as … as (as tall as).", ['Mas matanda siya sa akin.', 'Ito ang pinakamagandang pelikula ngayong taon.']),
},
'some-any': {
 'es': ('Some, any, much, many', "«Some» en frases afirmativas (I have some money), «any» en negaciones y preguntas (I don't have any money. Do you have any money?).\n«Much» con incontables (much water), «many» con contables (many books), «a lot of» con ambos.\nA few (unos pocos, contable), a little (un poco, incontable).", ['¿Quiere té?', 'No hay mucha gente.']),
 'de': ('Some, any, much, many', "„Some“ in bejahten Sätzen (I have some money), „any“ in Verneinungen und Fragen (I don't have any money. Do you have any money?).\n„Much“ bei Unzählbarem (much water), „many“ bei Zählbarem (many books), „a lot of“ bei beidem.\nA few (ein paar, zählbar), a little (ein wenig, unzählbar).", ['Möchten Sie Tee?', 'Es sind nicht viele Leute da.']),
 'it': ('Some, any, much, many', "«Some» nelle frasi affermative (I have some money), «any» nelle negazioni e nelle domande (I don't have any money. Do you have any money?).\n«Much» con i non numerabili (much water), «many» con i numerabili (many books), «a lot of» con entrambi.\nA few (alcuni, numerabile), a little (un po', non numerabile).", ['Vuole del tè?', "Non c'è molta gente."]),
 'pt': ('Some, any, much, many', "«Some» em frases afirmativas (I have some money), «any» em negações e perguntas (I don't have any money. Do you have any money?).\n«Much» com incontáveis (much water), «many» com contáveis (many books), «a lot of» com ambos.\nA few (alguns, contável), a little (um pouco, incontável).", ['Quer chá?', 'Não há muita gente.']),
 'ja': ('some, any, much, many', "肯定文では「some」（I have some money）、否定文と疑問文では「any」（I don't have any money. Do you have any money?）。\n数えられないものには「much」（much water）、数えられるものには「many」（many books）、両方に「a lot of」。\na few（少しの、可算）、a little（少しの、不可算）。", ['お茶はいかがですか？', '人はあまりいません。']),
 'zh': ('some、any、much、many', "肯定句用「some」（I have some money），否定句和疑问句用「any」（I don't have any money. Do you have any money?）。\n不可数名词用「much」（much water），可数名词用「many」（many books），两者都可用「a lot of」。\na few（几个，可数），a little（一点，不可数）。", ['要喝点茶吗？', '人不多。']),
 'ko': ('some, any, much, many', "긍정문에는 「some」(I have some money), 부정문과 의문문에는 「any」(I don't have any money. Do you have any money?).\n셀 수 없는 것에는 「much」(much water), 셀 수 있는 것에는 「many」(many books), 둘 다에 「a lot of」.\na few(몇몇, 가산), a little(조금, 불가산).", ['차 드실래요?', '사람이 많지 않아요.']),
 'lt': ('Some, any, much, many', "„Some“ teigiamuose sakiniuose (I have some money), „any“ neigiamuose ir klausiamuose (I don't have any money. Do you have any money?).\n„Much“ su neskaičiuojamais (much water), „many“ su skaičiuojamais (many books), „a lot of“ su abiem.\nA few (keli, skaičiuojami), a little (truputis, neskaičiuojami).", ['Ar norėtumėte arbatos?', 'Žmonių nedaug.']),
 'tl': ('Some, any, much, many', "«Some» sa pangungusap na apirmatibo (I have some money), «any» sa negatibo at tanong (I don't have any money. Do you have any money?).\n«Much» sa di-mabibilang (much water), «many» sa mabibilang (many books), «a lot of» sa pareho.\nA few (ilang, mabibilang), a little (kaunti, di-mabibilang).", ['Gusto mo ba ng tsaa?', 'Hindi gaanong marami ang tao.']),
},
'present-perfect': {
 'es': ('El present perfect', "have / has + participio (worked, seen, been, done). Une el pasado con el presente: experiencia (I have been to Japan), acción reciente cuyo resultado importa (I've lost my keys), situación que sigue con for / since (I have lived here for ten years / since 2015).\nCon una fecha pasada precisa (yesterday, in 2010) se usa el pasado simple, no el present perfect.", ['¿Has comido sushi alguna vez?', 'Acaba de llegar.']),
 'de': ('Das Present Perfect', "have / has + Partizip (worked, seen, been, done). Es verbindet Vergangenheit und Gegenwart: Erfahrung (I have been to Japan), kürzlich Geschehenes mit Folgen (I've lost my keys), andauernde Situation mit for / since (I have lived here for ten years / since 2015).\nMit genauer Zeitangabe in der Vergangenheit (yesterday, in 2010) steht das Simple Past.", ['Hast du schon einmal Sushi gegessen?', 'Er ist gerade angekommen.']),
 'it': ('Il present perfect', "have / has + participio (worked, seen, been, done). Collega passato e presente: esperienza (I have been to Japan), azione recente di cui conta il risultato (I've lost my keys), situazione che dura ancora con for / since (I have lived here for ten years / since 2015).\nCon una data passata precisa (yesterday, in 2010) si usa il past simple.", ['Hai mai mangiato il sushi?', 'È appena arrivato.']),
 'pt': ('O present perfect', "have / has + particípio (worked, seen, been, done). Liga o passado ao presente: experiência (I have been to Japan), ação recente cujo resultado importa (I've lost my keys), situação que continua com for / since (I have lived here for ten years / since 2015).\nCom uma data passada precisa (yesterday, in 2010) usa-se o past simple.", ['Você já comeu sushi?', 'Ele acabou de chegar.']),
 'ja': ('現在完了形', "have / has + 過去分詞（worked, seen, been, done）。過去と現在をつなぎます：経験（I have been to Japan）、結果が残る最近の動作（I've lost my keys）、for / since で今も続く状態（I have lived here for ten years / since 2015）。\n過去のはっきりした時（yesterday, in 2010）がある場合は過去形を使います。", ['お寿司を食べたことがありますか？', '彼はちょうど着いたところです。']),
 'zh': ('现在完成时', "have / has + 过去分词（worked, seen, been, done）。连接过去和现在：经历（I have been to Japan），结果仍有影响的最近动作（I've lost my keys），用 for / since 表示持续到现在的情况（I have lived here for ten years / since 2015）。\n有明确的过去时间（yesterday, in 2010）时用一般过去时。", ['你吃过寿司吗？', '他刚到。']),
 'ko': ('현재완료', "have / has + 과거분사(worked, seen, been, done). 과거와 현재를 이어 줍니다: 경험(I have been to Japan), 결과가 남아 있는 최근 동작(I've lost my keys), for / since로 지금까지 계속되는 상황(I have lived here for ten years / since 2015).\n분명한 과거 시점(yesterday, in 2010)이 있으면 과거형을 씁니다.", ['초밥 먹어 본 적 있어요?', '그는 방금 도착했어요.']),
 'lt': ('Esamasis atliktinis laikas', "have / has + dalyvis (worked, seen, been, done). Jis jungia praeitį su dabartimi: patirtis (I have been to Japan), neseniai įvykęs veiksmas su pasekme (I've lost my keys), tebesitęsianti būsena su for / since (I have lived here for ten years / since 2015).\nSu tikslia praeities data (yesterday, in 2010) vartojamas paprastasis būtasis laikas.", ['Ar kada nors valgei suši?', 'Jis ką tik atvyko.']),
 'tl': ('Ang present perfect', "have / has + participle (worked, seen, been, done). Pinag-uugnay nito ang nakaraan at kasalukuyan: karanasan (I have been to Japan), bagong kilos na mahalaga ang resulta (I've lost my keys), kalagayang nagpapatuloy gamit ang for / since (I have lived here for ten years / since 2015).\nKapag may tiyak na oras sa nakaraan (yesterday, in 2010), past simple ang gamit.", ['Nakakain ka na ba ng sushi?', 'Kararating lang niya.']),
},
'modals': {
 'es': ('Obligación y consejo: must, have to, should', "«Must» y «have to» expresan obligación (You must stop. I have to work). Cuidado con las negaciones: mustn't = prohibición, don't have to = no es necesario.\n«Should» da un consejo (You should rest). «May» y «might» expresan posibilidad (It might rain).\nLos modales van seguidos del verbo sin «to» y no llevan -s.", ['Deberías ir al médico.', 'No tienes que venir.']),
 'de': ('Pflicht und Rat: must, have to, should', "„Must“ und „have to“ drücken Pflicht aus (You must stop. I have to work). Vorsicht bei der Verneinung: mustn't = Verbot, don't have to = nicht nötig.\n„Should“ gibt einen Rat (You should rest). „May“ und „might“ drücken Möglichkeit aus (It might rain).\nModalverben stehen mit dem Verb ohne „to“ und bekommen kein -s.", ['Du solltest zum Arzt gehen.', 'Du musst nicht kommen.']),
 'it': ('Obbligo e consiglio: must, have to, should', "«Must» e «have to» esprimono obbligo (You must stop. I have to work). Attenzione alle negazioni: mustn't = divieto, don't have to = non è necessario.\n«Should» dà un consiglio (You should rest). «May» e «might» esprimono possibilità (It might rain).\nI modali sono seguiti dal verbo senza «to» e non prendono la -s.", ['Dovresti andare dal medico.', 'Non sei obbligato a venire.']),
 'pt': ('Obrigação e conselho: must, have to, should', "«Must» e «have to» expressam obrigação (You must stop. I have to work). Cuidado com as negações: mustn't = proibição, don't have to = não é necessário.\n«Should» dá um conselho (You should rest). «May» e «might» expressam possibilidade (It might rain).\nOs modais são seguidos do verbo sem «to» e não levam -s.", ['Você deveria ir ao médico.', 'Você não precisa vir.']),
 'ja': ('義務と助言：must, have to, should', "must と have to は義務を表します（You must stop. I have to work）。否定に注意：mustn't は禁止、don't have to は「〜しなくてよい」。\nshould は助言（You should rest）。may と might は可能性（It might rain）。\n助動詞の後ろは to のない動詞で、-s はつきません。", ['医者に診てもらったほうがいいですよ。', '来なくてもいいですよ。']),
 'zh': ('义务和建议：must、have to、should', "must 和 have to 表示义务（You must stop. I have to work）。注意否定：mustn't 表示禁止，don't have to 表示不必。\nshould 表示建议（You should rest）。may 和 might 表示可能（It might rain）。\n情态动词后接不带 to 的动词，本身不加 -s。", ['你应该去看医生。', '你不必来。']),
 'ko': ('의무와 조언: must, have to, should', "must와 have to는 의무를 나타냅니다(You must stop. I have to work). 부정에 주의: mustn't는 금지, don't have to는 '~할 필요 없다'.\nshould는 조언(You should rest). may와 might는 가능성(It might rain).\n조동사 뒤에는 to 없는 동사가 오며 -s가 붙지 않습니다.", ['병원에 가 보는 게 좋겠어요.', '안 와도 돼요.']),
 'lt': ('Prievolė ir patarimas: must, have to, should', "„Must“ ir „have to“ reiškia prievolę (You must stop. I have to work). Atsargiai su neiginiais: mustn't = draudimas, don't have to = nebūtina.\n„Should“ duoda patarimą (You should rest). „May“ ir „might“ reiškia galimybę (It might rain).\nPo modalinių veiksmažodžių eina veiksmažodis be „to“, jie negauna -s.", ['Turėtum nueiti pas gydytoją.', 'Tau nebūtina ateiti.']),
 'tl': ('Obligasyon at payo: must, have to, should', "Ang «must» at «have to» ay obligasyon (You must stop. I have to work). Mag-ingat sa negatibo: mustn't = pagbabawal, don't have to = hindi kailangan.\nAng «should» ay payo (You should rest). Ang «may» at «might» ay posibilidad (It might rain).\nSinusundan ang mga modal ng pandiwang walang «to» at walang -s.", ['Dapat kang magpatingin sa doktor.', 'Hindi mo kailangang pumunta.']),
},
'conditional-1': {
 'es': ('Las frases con if (real)', "Condición posible: if + presente, will + verbo. If it rains, I will stay at home. Nunca se pone «will» después de if.\nVerdad general: if + presente, presente. If you heat ice, it melts.\n«Unless» = if … not; «when» para lo que es seguro.", ['Si estudias, aprobarás.']),
 'de': ('Bedingungssätze mit if (real)', "Mögliche Bedingung: if + Präsens, will + Verb. If it rains, I will stay at home. Nach if steht nie „will“.\nAllgemeine Wahrheit: if + Präsens, Präsens. If you heat ice, it melts.\n„Unless“ = if … not; „when“ für Sicheres.", ['Wenn du lernst, bestehst du.']),
 'it': ('Le frasi con if (reale)', "Condizione possibile: if + presente, will + verbo. If it rains, I will stay at home. Mai «will» dopo if.\nVerità generale: if + presente, presente. If you heat ice, it melts.\n«Unless» = if … not; «when» per ciò che è certo.", ['Se studi, passerai.']),
 'pt': ('As frases com if (real)', "Condição possível: if + presente, will + verbo. If it rains, I will stay at home. Nunca se usa «will» depois de if.\nVerdade geral: if + presente, presente. If you heat ice, it melts.\n«Unless» = if … not; «when» para o que é certo.", ['Se você estudar, vai passar.']),
 'ja': ('if を使う条件文（現実）', "起こりうる条件：if + 現在形、will + 動詞。If it rains, I will stay at home。if の後に will は使いません。\n一般的な真理：if + 現在形、現在形。If you heat ice, it melts。\nunless は「if … not」、確実なことには when を使います。", ['勉強すれば合格しますよ。']),
 'zh': ('if 条件句（真实条件）', "可能的条件：if + 一般现在时，will + 动词。If it rains, I will stay at home。if 后面不用 will。\n普遍真理：if + 一般现在时，一般现在时。If you heat ice, it melts。\nunless = if … not；确定会发生的事用 when。", ['如果你学习，你就会通过。']),
 'ko': ('if 조건문 (현실)', "가능한 조건: if + 현재형, will + 동사. If it rains, I will stay at home. if 뒤에는 절대 will을 쓰지 않습니다.\n일반적인 진리: if + 현재형, 현재형. If you heat ice, it melts.\nunless = if … not, 확실한 일에는 when을 씁니다.", ['공부하면 합격할 거예요.']),
 'lt': ('Sąlygos sakiniai su if (realūs)', "Galima sąlyga: if + esamasis laikas, will + veiksmažodis. If it rains, I will stay at home. Po if niekada nevartojamas „will“.\nBendra tiesa: if + esamasis, esamasis. If you heat ice, it melts.\n„Unless“ = if … not; „when“ – tam, kas tikra.", ['Jei mokysiesi, išlaikysi.']),
 'tl': ('Mga pangungusap na may if (totoo)', "Posibleng kondisyon: if + kasalukuyan, will + pandiwa. If it rains, I will stay at home. Hindi kailanman ginagamit ang «will» pagkatapos ng if.\nPangkalahatang katotohanan: if + kasalukuyan, kasalukuyan. If you heat ice, it melts.\nAng «unless» = if … not; «when» para sa tiyak.", ['Kung mag-aaral ka, papasa ka.']),
},
'relatives': {
 'es': ('Las relativas: who, which, that', "«Who» para personas, «which» para cosas, «that» para ambas en el lenguaje corriente. «Whose» = cuyo (posesión), «where» para un lugar.\nCuando el pronombre es complemento se puede omitir: the book (that) I read.", ['El hombre que vive al lado es médico.', 'Esta es la casa donde nací.']),
 'de': ('Relativsätze: who, which, that', "„Who“ für Personen, „which“ für Dinge, „that“ umgangssprachlich für beides. „Whose“ = dessen / deren, „where“ für einen Ort.\nIst das Pronomen Objekt, kann es entfallen: the book (that) I read.", ['Der Mann, der nebenan wohnt, ist Arzt.', 'Das ist das Haus, in dem ich geboren wurde.']),
 'it': ('Le relative: who, which, that', "«Who» per le persone, «which» per le cose, «that» per entrambe nella lingua corrente. «Whose» = il cui (possesso), «where» per un luogo.\nQuando il pronome è complemento si può omettere: the book (that) I read.", ["L'uomo che abita accanto è medico.", 'Questa è la casa dove sono nato.']),
 'pt': ('As relativas: who, which, that', "«Who» para pessoas, «which» para coisas, «that» para ambas na língua corrente. «Whose» = cujo (posse), «where» para um lugar.\nQuando o pronome é complemento pode ser omitido: the book (that) I read.", ['O homem que mora ao lado é médico.', 'Esta é a casa onde nasci.']),
 'ja': ('関係詞：who, which, that', "人には who、物には which、話し言葉ではどちらにも that を使います。whose は所有、where は場所を表します。\n関係代名詞が目的語のときは省略できます：the book (that) I read。", ['隣に住んでいる男性は医者です。', 'これは私が生まれた家です。']),
 'zh': ('关系从句：who、which、that', "人用 who，物用 which，口语中两者都可用 that。whose 表示所属，where 表示地点。\n关系代词作宾语时可以省略：the book (that) I read。", ['住在隔壁的那个人是医生。', '这是我出生的房子。']),
 'ko': ('관계사: who, which, that', "사람에는 who, 사물에는 which, 일상 회화에서는 둘 다 that을 씁니다. whose는 소유, where는 장소를 나타냅니다.\n관계대명사가 목적어일 때는 생략할 수 있습니다: the book (that) I read.", ['옆집에 사는 남자는 의사예요.', '여기가 제가 태어난 집이에요.']),
 'lt': ('Šalutiniai pažyminio sakiniai: who, which, that', "„Who“ žmonėms, „which“ daiktams, „that“ šnekamojoje kalboje abiem. „Whose“ = kurio (priklausomybė), „where“ vietai.\nKai įvardis yra papildinys, jį galima praleisti: the book (that) I read.", ['Vyras, kuris gyvena šalia, yra gydytojas.', 'Tai namas, kuriame gimiau.']),
 'tl': ('Mga sugnay na pang-uri: who, which, that', "«Who» para sa tao, «which» para sa bagay, «that» para sa pareho sa karaniwang usapan. «Whose» = na may-ari, «where» para sa lugar.\nKapag layon ang panghalip, puwedeng alisin: the book (that) I read.", ['Doktor ang lalaking nakatira sa tabi.', 'Ito ang bahay kung saan ako ipinanganak.']),
},
'passive': {
 'es': ('La voz pasiva', "be + participio: The window was broken. El agente se introduce con «by» (by a child).\n«Be» se conjuga en el tiempo necesario: is made, was made, has been made, will be made.\nEl inglés usa la pasiva mucho más que el español: I was told… = me dijeron…", ['Este libro fue escrito en 1950.', 'Aquí se habla inglés.']),
 'de': ('Das Passiv', "be + Partizip: The window was broken. Der Urheber wird mit „by“ angeschlossen (by a child).\n„Be“ steht in der gewünschten Zeit: is made, was made, has been made, will be made.\nDas Englische benutzt das Passiv oft, wo man im Deutschen „man“ sagt: I was told… = man hat mir gesagt…", ['Dieses Buch wurde 1950 geschrieben.', 'Hier wird Englisch gesprochen.']),
 'it': ('Il passivo', "be + participio: The window was broken. L'agente è introdotto da «by» (by a child).\n«Be» si coniuga al tempo voluto: is made, was made, has been made, will be made.\nL'inglese usa il passivo molto più dell'italiano: I was told… = mi hanno detto…", ['Questo libro è stato scritto nel 1950.', 'Qui si parla inglese.']),
 'pt': ('A voz passiva', "be + particípio: The window was broken. O agente é introduzido por «by» (by a child).\n«Be» conjuga-se no tempo necessário: is made, was made, has been made, will be made.\nO inglês usa a passiva muito mais que o português: I was told… = disseram-me…", ['Este livro foi escrito em 1950.', 'Aqui se fala inglês.']),
 'ja': ('受動態', "be + 過去分詞：The window was broken。動作をする人は by で示します（by a child）。\nbe を必要な時制にします：is made, was made, has been made, will be made。\n英語は受動態をよく使います：I was told…＝〜と言われた。", ['この本は1950年に書かれました。', 'ここでは英語が話されています。']),
 'zh': ('被动语态', "be + 过去分词：The window was broken。动作执行者用 by 引出（by a child）。\nbe 按需要的时态变化：is made，was made，has been made，will be made。\n英语比汉语更常用被动：I was told… = 有人告诉我……", ['这本书写于1950年。', '这里说英语。']),
 'ko': ('수동태', "be + 과거분사: The window was broken. 행위자는 by로 나타냅니다(by a child).\nbe를 필요한 시제로 바꿉니다: is made, was made, has been made, will be made.\n영어는 수동태를 자주 씁니다: I was told… = ~라고 들었다.", ['이 책은 1950년에 쓰였어요.', '여기서는 영어를 써요.']),
 'lt': ('Neveikiamoji rūšis', "be + dalyvis: The window was broken. Veikėjas įvedamas su „by“ (by a child).\n„Be“ asmenuojamas reikiamu laiku: is made, was made, has been made, will be made.\nAnglai neveikiamąją rūšį vartoja dažnai: I was told… = man pasakė…", ['Ši knyga parašyta 1950 metais.', 'Čia kalbama angliškai.']),
 'tl': ('Ang balintiyak (passive)', "be + participle: The window was broken. Ipinapakilala ang gumawa gamit ang «by» (by a child).\nBinabanghay ang «be» sa kailangang panahunan: is made, was made, has been made, will be made.\nMadalas gamitin ng Ingles ang passive: I was told… = sinabihan ako…", ['Isinulat ang librong ito noong 1950.', 'Ingles ang sinasalita rito.']),
},
'conditional-2': {
 'es': ('Lo irreal: would y would have', "Irreal de presente: if + pasado simple, would + verbo. If I had more time, I would travel. Con be se dice were en todas las personas: If I were you…\nIrreal de pasado: if + had + participio, would have + participio. If I had known, I would have come.\n«I wish» sigue la misma lógica: I wish I were rich. I wish I had studied.", ['Yo que tú, aceptaría.', 'Habría ayudado si me lo hubieras pedido.']),
 'de': ('Das Irreale: would und would have', "Irreale Gegenwart: if + Simple Past, would + Verb. If I had more time, I would travel. Bei be sagt man were in allen Personen: If I were you…\nIrreale Vergangenheit: if + had + Partizip, would have + Partizip. If I had known, I would have come.\n„I wish“ folgt derselben Logik: I wish I were rich. I wish I had studied.", ['An deiner Stelle würde ich annehmen.', 'Ich hätte geholfen, wenn du gefragt hättest.']),
 'it': ("L'irreale: would e would have", "Irreale del presente: if + past simple, would + verbo. If I had more time, I would travel. Con be si dice were a tutte le persone: If I were you…\nIrreale del passato: if + had + participio, would have + participio. If I had known, I would have come.\n«I wish» segue la stessa logica: I wish I were rich. I wish I had studied.", ['Al tuo posto accetterei.', 'Avrei aiutato se me lo avessi chiesto.']),
 'pt': ('O irreal: would e would have', "Irreal do presente: if + past simple, would + verbo. If I had more time, I would travel. Com be diz-se were em todas as pessoas: If I were you…\nIrreal do passado: if + had + particípio, would have + particípio. If I had known, I would have come.\n«I wish» segue a mesma lógica: I wish I were rich. I wish I had studied.", ['No seu lugar, eu aceitaria.', 'Eu teria ajudado se você tivesse pedido.']),
 'ja': ('仮定法：would と would have', "現在の事実に反する仮定：if + 過去形、would + 動詞。If I had more time, I would travel。be はどの人称でも were：If I were you…\n過去の事実に反する仮定：if + had + 過去分詞、would have + 過去分詞。If I had known, I would have come。\nI wish も同じ考え方です：I wish I were rich. I wish I had studied。", ['私があなたなら、引き受けます。', '頼まれていたら手伝ったのに。']),
 'zh': ('虚拟语气：would 与 would have', "与现在事实相反：if + 一般过去时，would + 动词。If I had more time, I would travel。be 在所有人称都用 were：If I were you…\n与过去事实相反：if + had + 过去分词，would have + 过去分词。If I had known, I would have come。\nI wish 用法相同：I wish I were rich. I wish I had studied。", ['如果我是你，我会接受。', '要是你开口，我早就帮忙了。']),
 'ko': ('가정법: would와 would have', "현재 사실의 반대: if + 과거형, would + 동사. If I had more time, I would travel. be는 모든 인칭에서 were: If I were you…\n과거 사실의 반대: if + had + 과거분사, would have + 과거분사. If I had known, I would have come.\nI wish도 같은 원리입니다: I wish I were rich. I wish I had studied.", ['제가 당신이라면 받아들이겠어요.', '부탁했으면 도와줬을 거예요.']),
 'lt': ('Nerealios sąlygos: would ir would have', "Nereali dabartis: if + paprastasis būtasis, would + veiksmažodis. If I had more time, I would travel. Su be visiems asmenims sakoma were: If I were you…\nNereali praeitis: if + had + dalyvis, would have + dalyvis. If I had known, I would have come.\n„I wish“ remiasi ta pačia logika: I wish I were rich. I wish I had studied.", ['Tavo vietoje sutikčiau.', 'Būčiau padėjęs, jei būtum paprašęs.']),
 'tl': ('Di-totoong kondisyon: would at would have', "Di-totoo sa kasalukuyan: if + past simple, would + pandiwa. If I had more time, I would travel. Sa be, «were» sa lahat ng panauhan: If I were you…\nDi-totoo sa nakaraan: if + had + participle, would have + participle. If I had known, I would have come.\nGanito rin ang «I wish»: I wish I were rich. I wish I had studied.", ['Kung ako ikaw, tatanggapin ko.', 'Tumulong sana ako kung humingi ka.']),
},
'gerund-infinitive': {
 'es': ('¿Verbo en -ing o infinitivo?', "Algunos verbos van seguidos de -ing: enjoy, finish, avoid, mind, keep, suggest (I enjoy reading). Otros de to + verbo: want, decide, hope, need, promise, learn (I want to go).\nTras una preposición, siempre -ing: before leaving, good at cooking.\nStop doing = dejar de hacer; stop to do = pararse para hacer. Remember doing = recordar haber hecho; remember to do = acordarse de hacer.", ['Ella decidió irse.', 'Me gusta cocinar.']),
 'de': ('Verb mit -ing oder Infinitiv?', "Manche Verben stehen mit -ing: enjoy, finish, avoid, mind, keep, suggest (I enjoy reading). Andere mit to + Verb: want, decide, hope, need, promise, learn (I want to go).\nNach einer Präposition immer -ing: before leaving, good at cooking.\nStop doing = aufhören zu tun; stop to do = anhalten, um zu tun. Remember doing = sich erinnern, etwas getan zu haben; remember to do = daran denken, etwas zu tun.", ['Sie beschloss zu gehen.', 'Ich koche gern.']),
 'it': ('Verbo in -ing o infinito?', "Alcuni verbi sono seguiti da -ing: enjoy, finish, avoid, mind, keep, suggest (I enjoy reading). Altri da to + verbo: want, decide, hope, need, promise, learn (I want to go).\nDopo una preposizione sempre -ing: before leaving, good at cooking.\nStop doing = smettere di fare; stop to do = fermarsi per fare. Remember doing = ricordare di aver fatto; remember to do = ricordarsi di fare.", ['Ha deciso di andarsene.', 'Mi piace cucinare.']),
 'pt': ('Verbo em -ing ou infinitivo?', "Alguns verbos são seguidos de -ing: enjoy, finish, avoid, mind, keep, suggest (I enjoy reading). Outros de to + verbo: want, decide, hope, need, promise, learn (I want to go).\nDepois de preposição, sempre -ing: before leaving, good at cooking.\nStop doing = parar de fazer; stop to do = parar para fazer. Remember doing = lembrar de ter feito; remember to do = lembrar-se de fazer.", ['Ela decidiu ir embora.', 'Gosto de cozinhar.']),
 'ja': ('-ing 形か不定詞か', "-ing 形をとる動詞：enjoy, finish, avoid, mind, keep, suggest（I enjoy reading）。to + 動詞をとる動詞：want, decide, hope, need, promise, learn（I want to go）。\n前置詞の後は必ず -ing：before leaving, good at cooking。\nstop doing = 〜するのをやめる、stop to do = 〜するために立ち止まる。remember doing = 〜したことを覚えている、remember to do = 忘れずに〜する。", ['彼女は去ることに決めました。', '料理するのが好きです。']),
 'zh': ('动名词还是不定式？', "有些动词后接 -ing：enjoy, finish, avoid, mind, keep, suggest（I enjoy reading）。有些后接 to + 动词：want, decide, hope, need, promise, learn（I want to go）。\n介词后总是用 -ing：before leaving, good at cooking。\nstop doing = 停止做某事；stop to do = 停下来去做某事。remember doing = 记得做过；remember to do = 记得要做。", ['她决定离开。', '我喜欢做饭。']),
 'ko': ('-ing인가 to부정사인가?', "-ing를 쓰는 동사: enjoy, finish, avoid, mind, keep, suggest (I enjoy reading). to + 동사를 쓰는 동사: want, decide, hope, need, promise, learn (I want to go).\n전치사 뒤에는 항상 -ing: before leaving, good at cooking.\nstop doing = ~하는 것을 그만두다, stop to do = ~하려고 멈추다. remember doing = ~한 것을 기억하다, remember to do = 잊지 않고 ~하다.", ['그녀는 떠나기로 했어요.', '저는 요리하는 걸 좋아해요.']),
 'lt': ('-ing forma ar bendratis?', "Po kai kurių veiksmažodžių eina -ing: enjoy, finish, avoid, mind, keep, suggest (I enjoy reading). Po kitų – to + veiksmažodis: want, decide, hope, need, promise, learn (I want to go).\nPo prielinksnio visada -ing: before leaving, good at cooking.\nStop doing = liautis daryti; stop to do = sustoti, kad padarytum. Remember doing = prisiminti, kad padarei; remember to do = nepamiršti padaryti.", ['Ji nusprendė išeiti.', 'Man patinka gaminti.']),
 'tl': ('Pandiwang -ing o infinitive?', "May mga pandiwang sinusundan ng -ing: enjoy, finish, avoid, mind, keep, suggest (I enjoy reading). Ang iba ay ng to + pandiwa: want, decide, hope, need, promise, learn (I want to go).\nPagkatapos ng pang-ukol, laging -ing: before leaving, good at cooking.\nStop doing = tumigil sa paggawa; stop to do = huminto para gawin. Remember doing = maalala na ginawa; remember to do = huwag kalimutang gawin.", ['Nagpasya siyang umalis.', 'Mahilig akong magluto.']),
},
'reported': {
 'es': ('El estilo indirecto', "Cuando el verbo introductor está en pasado, los tiempos retroceden un paso: presente → pasado (\"I am tired\" → He said he was tired), pasado → past perfect, will → would, can → could.\n«Say» (decir algo) / «tell» + persona (He told me that…).\nPregunta indirecta: orden sujeto-verbo, sin do: She asked where I lived.", ['Dijo que estaba ocupado.', 'Me dijo que vendría.']),
 'de': ('Die indirekte Rede', "Steht das einleitende Verb in der Vergangenheit, rücken die Zeiten eine Stufe zurück: Präsens → Simple Past (\"I am tired\" → He said he was tired), Simple Past → Past Perfect, will → would, can → could.\n„Say“ (etwas sagen) / „tell“ + Person (He told me that…).\nIndirekte Frage: Subjekt vor Verb, ohne do: She asked where I lived.", ['Er sagte, er sei beschäftigt.', 'Sie sagte mir, dass sie kommen würde.']),
 'it': ('Il discorso indiretto', "Quando il verbo introduttivo è al passato, i tempi arretrano di un grado: presente → past simple (\"I am tired\" → He said he was tired), past simple → past perfect, will → would, can → could.\n«Say» (dire qualcosa) / «tell» + persona (He told me that…).\nDomanda indiretta: ordine soggetto-verbo, senza do: She asked where I lived.", ['Ha detto che era occupato.', 'Mi ha detto che sarebbe venuta.']),
 'pt': ('O discurso indireto', "Quando o verbo introdutor está no passado, os tempos recuam um grau: presente → past simple (\"I am tired\" → He said he was tired), past simple → past perfect, will → would, can → could.\n«Say» (dizer algo) / «tell» + pessoa (He told me that…).\nPergunta indireta: ordem sujeito-verbo, sem do: She asked where I lived.", ['Ele disse que estava ocupado.', 'Ela me disse que viria.']),
 'ja': ('間接話法', "伝える動詞が過去形のとき、時制が一つ過去にずれます：現在 → 過去（\"I am tired\" → He said he was tired）、過去 → 過去完了、will → would、can → could。\nsay（〜と言う）/ tell + 人（He told me that…）。\n間接疑問文は「主語＋動詞」の順で do は使いません：She asked where I lived。", ['彼は忙しいと言いました。', '彼女は来ると私に言いました。']),
 'zh': ('间接引语', "引述动词为过去时时，时态要往前推一步：现在时 → 过去时（\"I am tired\" → He said he was tired），过去时 → 过去完成时，will → would，can → could。\nsay（说某事）/ tell + 人（He told me that…）。\n间接疑问句用陈述语序，不用 do：She asked where I lived。", ['他说他很忙。', '她告诉我她会来。']),
 'ko': ('간접 화법', "전달 동사가 과거일 때 시제가 한 단계 과거로 바뀝니다: 현재 → 과거(\"I am tired\" → He said he was tired), 과거 → 과거완료, will → would, can → could.\nsay(~라고 말하다) / tell + 사람(He told me that…).\n간접 의문문은 주어 + 동사 순서이며 do를 쓰지 않습니다: She asked where I lived.", ['그는 바쁘다고 말했어요.', '그녀는 오겠다고 저에게 말했어요.']),
 'lt': ('Netiesioginė kalba', "Kai įvadinis veiksmažodis yra būtojo laiko, laikai pasislenka per vieną pakopą atgal: esamasis → būtasis (\"I am tired\" → He said he was tired), būtasis → būtasis atliktinis, will → would, can → could.\n„Say“ (pasakyti ką) / „tell“ + asmuo (He told me that…).\nNetiesioginis klausimas: veiksnys prieš veiksmažodį, be do: She asked where I lived.", ['Jis sakė, kad yra užsiėmęs.', 'Ji man pasakė, kad ateis.']),
 'tl': ('Di-tuwirang pananalita', "Kapag nasa nakaraan ang pandiwang nagpapakilala, umaatras ng isang hakbang ang panahunan: kasalukuyan → nakaraan (\"I am tired\" → He said he was tired), nakaraan → past perfect, will → would, can → could.\n«Say» (magsabi ng bagay) / «tell» + tao (He told me that…).\nDi-tuwirang tanong: simuno bago pandiwa, walang do: She asked where I lived.", ['Sinabi niyang abala siya.', 'Sinabi niya sa akin na darating siya.']),
},
'inversion': {
 'es': ('La inversión y el énfasis', "En estilo formal, un adverbio negativo al principio de la frase provoca la inversión: Never have I seen such a thing. Not only did he come, but he also helped. Hardly had we arrived when it started to rain.\nPara destacar un elemento se usa una frase escindida: It was John who called. What I need is a holiday.", ['Nunca he sido tan feliz.']),
 'de': ('Inversion und Hervorhebung', "Im gehobenen Stil führt ein verneinendes Adverb am Satzanfang zur Inversion: Never have I seen such a thing. Not only did he come, but he also helped. Hardly had we arrived when it started to rain.\nUm etwas hervorzuheben, benutzt man Spaltsätze: It was John who called. What I need is a holiday.", ['Nie war ich so glücklich.']),
 'it': ("L'inversione e l'enfasi", "Nello stile formale, un avverbio negativo all'inizio della frase provoca l'inversione: Never have I seen such a thing. Not only did he come, but he also helped. Hardly had we arrived when it started to rain.\nPer mettere in rilievo un elemento si usa la frase scissa: It was John who called. What I need is a holiday.", ['Non sono mai stato così felice.']),
 'pt': ('A inversão e a ênfase', "No estilo formal, um advérbio negativo no início da frase provoca inversão: Never have I seen such a thing. Not only did he come, but he also helped. Hardly had we arrived when it started to rain.\nPara destacar um elemento usa-se a frase clivada: It was John who called. What I need is a holiday.", ['Nunca fui tão feliz.']),
 'ja': ('倒置と強調', "改まった文体では、否定の副詞が文頭に来ると語順が倒置されます：Never have I seen such a thing. Not only did he come, but he also helped. Hardly had we arrived when it started to rain。\nある要素を強調するには分裂文を使います：It was John who called. What I need is a holiday。", ['こんなに幸せだったことはありません。']),
 'zh': ('倒装与强调', "在正式文体中，否定副词放在句首时要倒装：Never have I seen such a thing. Not only did he come, but he also helped. Hardly had we arrived when it started to rain。\n强调某一成分时用强调句：It was John who called. What I need is a holiday。", ['我从来没有这么幸福过。']),
 'ko': ('도치와 강조', "격식 있는 문체에서 부정 부사가 문장 앞에 오면 도치가 일어납니다: Never have I seen such a thing. Not only did he come, but he also helped. Hardly had we arrived when it started to rain.\n한 요소를 강조할 때는 분열문을 씁니다: It was John who called. What I need is a holiday.", ['이렇게 행복했던 적은 없어요.']),
 'lt': ('Inversija ir pabrėžimas', "Oficialiame stiliuje neigiamas prieveiksmis sakinio pradžioje sukelia inversiją: Never have I seen such a thing. Not only did he come, but he also helped. Hardly had we arrived when it started to rain.\nNorint pabrėžti dalį, vartojamas skaldytinis sakinys: It was John who called. What I need is a holiday.", ['Niekada nebuvau toks laimingas.']),
 'tl': ('Pagbaligtad at pagbibigay-diin', "Sa pormal na istilo, nagdudulot ng pagbaligtad ang negatibong pang-abay sa simula: Never have I seen such a thing. Not only did he come, but he also helped. Hardly had we arrived when it started to rain.\nPara bigyang-diin ang isang bahagi, gamitin ang cleft sentence: It was John who called. What I need is a holiday.", ['Hindi pa ako naging ganito kasaya.']),
},
}
